Package: Pando
Version: 1.5.0
Type: Package
Title: Inferring regulomes from multi-modal single-cell genomics data
Authors@R: person(given = "Jonas Simon",
               family = "Fleck",
               role = c("aut", "cre"),
               email = "jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch",
               comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4686-7254"))
Maintainer: Jonas Simon Fleck <jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch>
Description: Pando jointly uses scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq measurements to infer
    regulatory relationships between TF-binding site pairs and target genes.
    Condition-aware models use one exact TF-peak-target candidate supergraph and
    equal-condition within-condition variance scale. The default engine uses
    nested condition-stratified cell cross-fitting, sparse-group shared-support
    selection, and a support-constrained hierarchical-ridge refit.
    Standard Pando networks remain the compatibility surface. Absolute
    condition coefficients, shared coefficients, condition deviations,
    estimability, activity, transformation, direction, and single-cell
    projection layers are exposed through the single canonical
    pando_condition_grn_fit contract for reproducible downstream metacell
    comparisons. Version-suffixed condition-fit schemas are not public APIs.
    The public and stored contract contains no reference-condition coefficient,
    reference contrast, or comparison mask; conditions are compared directly on
    the shared equal-condition coordinate.
